{docstring Infomaterial.Relational.Spacetime.Boundary.Infohole.EventHorizon.event_surface_interior}

## Bundled Infohole

The full causal carrier bundles the causal set, readout region, and an effect
relation whose sources are shrouded:

{docstring Infomaterial.Relational.Spacetime.Boundary.Infohole.Infohole}

The canonical constructor uses shroud-local causal adjacency as its effect
relation:

{docstring Infomaterial.Relational.Spacetime.Boundary.Infohole.Infohole.ofReadout}

It carries its event horizon directly:

{docstring Infomaterial.Relational.Spacetime.Boundary.Infohole.Infohole.eventHorizon}

Its public laws expose the future-closed interior and the shroud support of
effects:

{docstring Infomaterial.Relational.Spacetime.Boundary.Infohole.Infohole.interior_future_closed}

{docstring Infomaterial.Relational.Spacetime.Boundary.Infohole.Infohole.interior_no_future_to_exterior}

{docstring Infomaterial.Relational.Spacetime.Boundary.Infohole.Infohole.shroud_exterior_predecessor}

{docstring Infomaterial.Relational.Spacetime.Boundary.Infohole.Infohole.effect_source_in_shroud}

## Generated Object, Generated Phenomenon

This is the first place where "infohole" is a settled object-name, but the
object-name is not free. The generated ascent is:

* process: causal reachability to a chosen readout;
* structure: the partition into no-readout interior, readout exterior, and
  shroud;
* force-site: an effect relation whose sources are restricted to the shroud;
* object: the bundled `Infohole`;
* phenomenon: effects can occur only from the generated boundary side.

The last line is checked rather than asserted by analogy:

{docstring Infomaterial.Relational.Spacetime.Boundary.Infohole.Infohole.effect_source_interior}

{docstring Infomaterial.Relational.Spacetime.Boundary.Infohole.Infohole.effect_source_not_exterior}

and for the canonical no-readout object:

{docstring Infomaterial.Relational.Spacetime.Boundary.Infohole.Infohole.ofReadout_effect_source_interior}

{docstring Infomaterial.Relational.Spacetime.Boundary.Infohole.Infohole.ofReadout_effect_source_not_exterior}

Checked:

```lean
example {E : Type} (H : Infohole E) {x y : E}
    (h : H.effect x y) :
    H.interior x :=
  H.effect_source_interior h

example {E : Type} (H : Infohole E) {x y : E}
    (h : H.effect x y) :
    Not (H.exterior x) :=
  H.effect_source_not_exterior h

example {E : Type} (C : CausalSet E) (readout : Region E)
    {x y : E}
    (h : (Infohole.ofReadout C readout).effect x y) :
    (Infohole.ofReadout C readout).interior x :=
  Infohole.ofReadout_effect_source_interior C readout h
```

This is the lawful "hole" reading in mereological language: the interior is not
an extra object placed inside an ambient container. It is the complement of
readout reachability, with a shroud where the surrounding causal structure can
encounter it. The effect law turns that boundary into a force-site, but it does
not yet prove entropy, area, Hawking radiation, information recovery, or smooth
horizon geometry.

## Phase Boundary

This is also the lawful boundary for any later "infohole matter" phrase. The
settled object is a finite no-readout carrier with a shroud and shroud-sourced
effects. Calling it a black-hole reading is a physical reading of that carrier,
not an additional theorem. Calling a horizon-bearing system an agent is likewise
frontier unless a later page constructs the transport from no-readout boundary
behavior to agency-bearing organization.

The page may therefore promote only this much: a causal region can fail to reach
readout; that no-readout region is future closed; its exterior is past closed;
the shroud is an interior boundary adjacent to the exterior; and bundled effects
must originate on that shroud side. The manual must not infer agency, entropy,
area, radiation, or recovery from the word "infohole."

## Repair Path

If this page overreaches, demote the claim to frontier unless the missing carrier
is built. A promotion path would add, in order: a lawful conformal-infinity
carrier, a boundary topology or smooth null-hypersurface carrier, an area
functional, and then thermodynamic or quantum-information structure. Until then,
the settled object is the no-readout closure site above.
